1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
So, if you want, you can fly higher.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Hinata!

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,000
What's up?

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Hey, man.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Hello, Kageyama!

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Hey! Hinata, Kageyama, you're both still alive!

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Hey, Yasuga.

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Yeah, hi.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
It's great to see you guys.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
So, hey, I hope you didn't start fighting the second you got back here.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,000
They did.

12
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
They were already going at it whenever I got here with the key.

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Aw, you two can't help yourselves.

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Hey, it's cool.

15
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Just you two dummies being yourselves, right?

16
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Kageyama, tell us how the big intensive went.

17
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Yeah, come on, man.

18
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
How was the all Japan stuff?

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
The floor wasn't made out of wood.

20
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
You're telling us about the court?

21
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
How was the volleyball, though, man?

22
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
There were stars from the whole country, right?

23
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Yes, and they were all really good.

24
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,000
That's the stuff.

25
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Tell me more!

26
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Hey, Hinata.

27
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
I thought you would sneak into the all Japan intensive.

28
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Well, I, uh...

29
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
He said he didn't because he didn't want to get arrested.

30
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Arrested?

31
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Tsukishima?

32
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
He told me he wanted to sneak into the Tokyo intensive.

33
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Didn't work out that way.

34
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Awesome, Hinata, think big!

35
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Did you do any growing while you were away, big guy?

36
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Yeah, I guess.

37
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Got a little taller, huh?

38
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,000
You his aunt or something?

39
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
He better not have gotten taller in five days.

40
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Hey!

41
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Hey!

42
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Yo!

43
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Hey!

44
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
I'm sorry for all the trouble that I caused.

45
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
I mean, even if you had been here, you'd have been worthless without me.

46
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Shut up, okay?

47
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,000
You don't have to keep saying it, man!

48
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,000
I know!

49
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
I believe I only said it that one time.

50
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Tsuki, is it me or have you grown some more?

51
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Shut up, Tadashi.

52
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Sure was quiet for a couple days anyway.

53
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,000
It sure was.

54
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Well, you're...

55
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,000
You're stupid!

56
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
All their fighting, it gives me a sense of peace.

57
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Oh, your butt stinks!

58
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Nice.

59
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Woods Town

60
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Alright, it's Western.

61
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Highlight here.

62
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:21,980
How did you do anything else?

63
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
That's Bars Today!

64
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:54,980
Thank you.

65
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:24,980
Thank you.

66
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:54,980
Thank you.

67
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:57,100
So, hey, uh, what's the tape for?

68
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:59,740
We're dividing the net into nine parts.

69
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:03,080
All last week, the team worked on improving their serves.

70
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:07,120
Coach told them to make sure they focus on where they want the ball to go

71
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:09,180
and that it'll go there whenever they hit it.

72
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:13,400
So when the ball passes over a part of the net, they should know where it'll fall.

73
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:22,200
Seventy percent.

74
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:28,880
Nice hit!

75
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:29,840
Hell yeah!

76
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:40,740
Easy!

77
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:42,120
Damn it!

78
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:43,160
Right at his ass.

79
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:54,500
Really?

80
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,220
Nishinoya couldn't handle that one?

81
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:59,560
He's not all that comfortable when he has to play overhand.

82
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,000
Then why not play underhand?

83
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,780
Why would he play overhand if he's not as comfortable with it?

84
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:08,060
The whole problem with jump floaters is that they're unpredictable.

85
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:14,360
The surest way to counter them is to position yourself further forward and catch the ball with an overhand pass.

86
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:20,200
And this spring, there's a good chance we'll find ourselves up against some servers who can hit some powerful jump floaters.

87
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:23,960
We're definitely going to need to find a few ways to counter them.

88
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:27,740
Hisashi, your serves are great!

89
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:28,320
I know!

90
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,540
Years coming along?

91
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:32,660
I think I'm going to play it safe and just stick to floaters for now.

92
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:35,420
I can do it too.

93
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:42,440
That's out.

94
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:47,760
Even Tadashi is working really hard.

95
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,200
That didn't feel right.

96
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:09,800
Is it out?

97
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:26,360
That Hinata...

98
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:27,180
Huh?

99
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:30,880
He can pull off some things athletically that seem superhuman sometimes.

100
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:33,360
But what he just did now...

101
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:35,360
It was almost...

102
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:35,860
Normal.

103
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:39,660
Great job, guys!

104
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:41,620
It's supposed to snow tonight.

105
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:42,640
Really?

106
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:43,960
Hey, uh, Kageyama.

107
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,640
What do you mean fly even higher?

108
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:47,720
Mmm.

109
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,320
Come on.

110
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:51,480
Hit some force with me.

111
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:55,140
Aren't you tired from all your training?

112
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:57,960
No overworking allowed, okay?

113
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,460
Just a few minutes longer?

114
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:02,260
Just a few minutes.

115
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:03,000
Right!

116
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:03,140
Right!

117
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:11,020
So when you jump, it's like, ba-boing!

118
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:12,260
Uh, what?

119
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,140
But a really good jump goes...

120
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:16,600
Boom!

121
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:17,540
See?

122
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:18,680
Hmm.

123
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:22,240
Your job is essentially to scurry around the court.

124
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:23,280
I don't scurry!

125
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:27,220
I would say it's your momentum that gives you that ba-boing jump.

126
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:31,120
Not that this is new, but his sound effects game is super weak.

127
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:33,760
It's been working out for us well enough.

128
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:36,480
And maybe that's the best you can do during an actual match.

129
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:37,280
That said...

130
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:40,840
If I know you, you can jump higher.

131
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:42,660
Tell me this.

132
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:45,960
Where do you typically hold most of your weight whenever you start to jump?

133
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,040
Uh, I don't know.

134
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:50,260
My feet?

135
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,540
Of course it's your feet!

136
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:52,840
Where else would it be, stupid?

137
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:55,440
Well, it's not like I ever paid much attention to it!

138
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:59,020
Are you trying to tell me that you can't jump in the air and think at the same time?

139
00:07:59,220 --> 00:07:59,660
Loser!

140
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:00,000
Wait!

141
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,780
Why am I getting yelled at right now?

142
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:05,780
Look.

143
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:09,540
High, stable jumps give you more freedom to react when you're in the air.

144
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:12,300
Those jumps...

145
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:13,800
Whenever you make them correctly,

146
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,400
you hear a sound when your feet leave the floor.

147
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:22,060
What are the odds they'll stop after a few minutes?

148
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,260
It could start snowing any second now.

149
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,720
Oh, come on, Daichi.

150
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,400
You actually believe those knuckleheads?

151
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,420
Shut up.

152
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:31,380
All clear?

153
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,120
Where's Hinata and Kageyama?

154
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:35,340
Said they'll be done in a few minutes.

155
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:37,560
They are something else.

156
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:38,800
What do you mean by that?

157
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:41,920
I can get that they're excited after coming back from training camp.

158
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:44,280
But if it were me, I'd want a break.

159
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:48,100
How much do you have to love volleyball to stay late after a full practice?

160
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,440
Yeah, well...

161
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,420
I feel like Kageyama's different.

162
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:54,780
He looked a bit more tense since he's gotten back.

163
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:56,700
Or maybe it's just me.

164
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:59,060
One more time!

165
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:03,740
Yeah.

166
00:09:04,260 --> 00:09:05,480
It's still awesome.

167
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:07,900
The height and position are perfect.

168
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:10,160
And he does it every single time.

169
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:11,940
He really is good.

170
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,940
Hey!

171
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:16,320
Your jump is drifting again!

172
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:20,320
You have to put more weight on the balls of your feet!

173
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,940
Actually paying attention to that will make a massive difference!

174
00:09:22,940 --> 00:09:25,020
Auuughhh!

175
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:31,660
Shift my weight!

176
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:33,780
The balls of my feet, and use the momentum to...!

177
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:35,020
象utness

178
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:36,040
Oh!

179
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:38,040
Jump!

180
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:42,040
Go home!

181
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:04,040
Nice kill!

182
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:08,040
Is something wrong?

183
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:10,040
Oh, no! Just thinking.

184
00:10:11,040 --> 00:10:16,040
Since Hinata got back from that training camp, there are moments when he gets super quiet.

185
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:26,040
You know, Tsukishima, when Koga Nagawa was setting balls for you, I think you were hitting it from higher up.

186
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:29,040
I'm jumping just like always.

187
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:32,040
Really? Maybe I just imagined it then.

188
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,040
Hm.

189
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:40,040
Kageyama.

190
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:44,040
Sir?

191
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:50,040
I know you said it's fine, but, I mean, uh, was it?

192
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,040
Hm?

193
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:54,040
It's just, uh, is there something bothering you?

194
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:56,040
No, sir.

195
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,040
No, sir.

196
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:58,040
Oh, okay.

197
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:04,040
What do you think it means to be a goody two-shoes?

198
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,040
Huh?

199
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,040
Oh.

200
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:09,040
Did somebody say that you were one?

201
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,040
Yeah, another setter at the intensive.

202
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:12,040
Of course.

203
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:13,040
Of course.

204
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:18,040
I should have known there'd be some shady characters at that intensive.

205
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:23,040
There is no better set than the one that is easy for the spiker to hit.

206
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,040
Huh?

207
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:27,040
My old man told me that a million times.

208
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:32,040
I think, really, that's all there is to say.

209
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:36,040
And that's one thing you'll never need to second guess.

210
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:37,040
Oh.

211
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:45,040
They should be here any minute now.

212
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:46,040
Yeah.

213
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,040
Yo, Asahi.

214
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:50,040
You better not be scared of them anymore.

215
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,040
Huh?

216
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:56,040
I couldn't ask for better opponents.

217
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:58,040
Haha.

218
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:01,040
I'm gonna try something.

219
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:02,040
Huh?

220
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,040
Day Tech!

221
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,040
Hello!

222
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:46,040
I see they're just as intimidating as ever.

223
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:51,040
There's no locking on today.

224
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,040
What's up, Hinata?

225
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,040
Kogane!

226
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:56,040
Ah! Suki!

227
00:12:58,040 --> 00:13:01,040
I want to thank you for coming out here today. We really appreciate it.

228
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:03,340
Congratulations on the Spring Nationals.

229
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:05,840
Our boys are really excited to play you today.

230
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:09,140
Thanks very much. And thanks again for your time.

231
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:18,440
Just because this is a practice match does not mean you hold back.

232
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:20,340
No way. Not on my watch.

233
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:24,740
Tsukishima, when Koga Nagawa was setting balls for you,

234
00:13:24,740 --> 00:13:26,440
I think you were hitting it from higher up.

235
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,740
Gather around, everyone!

236
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:39,940
Date Tech's blocking is without a doubt the best in the prefecture.

237
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:42,540
They may even be one of the best in the country.

238
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:46,540
And I hear they're even better since the Spring National Prelims.

239
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:50,740
Frankly, there's no way we have enough time to get our blocking skills

240
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:52,440
anywhere close to this team's level.

241
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:58,440
So listen, your job today is to play against Date Tech's new and improved defenses

242
00:13:58,940 --> 00:13:59,940
and get used to them.

243
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:03,940
That way, when you're blocked by similar walls on the Nationals,

244
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:05,940
you'll be able to keep your cool.

245
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:06,940
Right!

246
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:15,440
Texts for front.

247
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,440
Elite Command.

248
00:14:18,940 --> 00:14:19,940
Links.

249
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:20,940
Links.

250
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:25,940
Links.

251
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:26,640
Links.

252
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:29,640
tablespoons.

253
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,040
Mishidoya!

254
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:32,800
Go!

255
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:36,360
Yeah, dude!

256
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:38,860
Go!

257
00:14:38,860 --> 00:14:40,060
Yeah!

258
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:42,680
Bye!

259
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:43,780
Bye!

260
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:45,940
Paper 4 on esta Eddie's Chiangino!

261
00:14:45,940 --> 00:14:49,080
Let's play!

262
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:54,800
Is that Bingo?

263
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,240
Tight.

264
00:14:56,240 --> 00:15:01,480
Whoa, Hinata can move! Is this their infamous ultra-fast quick attack?

265
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:13,480
Barsch!

266
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:15,840
Read block!

267
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:28,360
Yikes! Our back row attack is so fast, they usually only have to deal with one blocker, if any.

268
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,320
I mean, we even used Hinata as a decoy.

269
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:36,640
But that block was practically all three of them.

270
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:41,020
They all blocked? Talk about fast reflexes!

271
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:48,520
It was just like Tsukishima in our game against Shiratorizawa.

272
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:51,260
Good blocking puts a lot of stress on the other team.

273
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:53,860
And not just on the spiker, but on the setter as well.

274
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:59,020
